WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:10.239
First, we consider the air conditioning requirements of a data center

2
00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.800
servers and other equipment generate a lot

3
00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:15.399
of heat which must be handled appropriately.

4
00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:18.959
This is not just to make it comfortable when humans are present

5
00:00:19.129 --> 00:00:22.739
but to ensure the equipment is kept within its operating parameters.

6
00:00:23.129 --> 00:00:28.000
When equipment gets too hot, it can lead to quicker failure or avoided warranty.

7
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.370
Most equipment is programmed to automatically shut down

8
00:00:31.379 --> 00:00:33.400
when a certain temperature threshold is met.

9
00:00:33.869 --> 00:00:36.680
This helps to protect the equipment but a system that

10
00:00:36.689 --> 00:00:39.319
is shut down is not available to the users.

11
00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:44.080
An abnormal system shutdown can also lead to the loss or corruption of data.

12
00:00:45.259 --> 00:00:47.360
Another consideration for the on premises

13
00:00:47.369 --> 00:00:50.110
data center is the fire suppression systems

14
00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.080
in the United States.

15
00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:54.909
Most commercial buildings are required to have sprinkler

16
00:00:54.919 --> 00:00:57.000
systems that are activated in a fire.

17
00:00:57.389 --> 00:01:00.389
These sprinklers minimize the amount of damage caused to the

18
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:04.069
building and keep the fire from spreading to adjacent areas,

19
00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:06.290
but they can be detrimental to electronic

20
00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:09.589
equipment as water and electricity don't mix

21
00:01:10.059 --> 00:01:13.110
while most water based fire suppression systems don't

22
00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:14.919
work like they do in the movies where

23
00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:18.959
a fire in one part of the building turns on the sprinklers for the entire building.

24
00:01:19.139 --> 00:01:22.680
Another hazard is having water overhead in a data center.

25
00:01:23.169 --> 00:01:26.559
Eventually water pipes will fail and may leak on equipment.

26
00:01:27.089 --> 00:01:30.870
This risk can be reduced somewhat by using a dry pipe system

27
00:01:30.949 --> 00:01:33.889
that keeps the water out of the pipes over the data center.

28
00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.150
These systems have a valve outside the data center that is

29
00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:40.500
only opened when a sensor indicates a fire is present.

30
00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:43.910
Since water is not held in the pipes above the data center,

31
00:01:43.919 --> 00:01:45.669
the risk of leaks is reduced.